Body:
I can reproduce this with matching versions:

- `opencode`: 1.17.13
- `@opencode-ai/sdk`: 1.17.13

Using the SDK:

```js
await client.session.promptAsync({
  sessionID,
  agent: "build",
  parts: [{ type: "text", text: "Return {\"ok\": true}" }],
  format: {
    type: "json_schema",
    schema: {
      type: "object",
      properties: { ok: { type: "boolean" } },
      required: ["ok"],
      additionalProperties: false,
    },
    retryCount: 2,
  },
});

const result = await client.session.messages({ sessionID });
```

`promptAsync` succeeds with HTTP 204, but `session.messages()` returns HTTP 400:

```text
Expected OutputFormatJsonSchema, got {"type":"json_schema","schema":...,"retryCount":2}
```

Using the same `format` with synchronous `session.prompt()` works and returns `info.structured`.

So it looks like the async prompt accepts the format, but the message listing endpoint later fails on it. This blocks SDK clients that use `promptAsync` + `session.messages()` with native structured output.

Hope this can be fixed soon. Thanks!

